{"title":"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 32","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The dimensions of a rectangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/3/8136a7ef6a03334a7246df9097e5bcc31ba33fd2.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$b$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f8abc0d69ac6ab491f6125f9550af6b25e22fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />. It is required to obtain a rectangle with dimensions <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/9/ec9eccc6ff90391b34a93c8c574f9737b990d95c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x &lt; a, y &lt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"95\" height=\"13\" />, \nso that its perimeter is one-third that of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, and its area is one-third that of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/f/f/eff43e84f8a3bcf7b6965f0a3248bc4d3a9d0cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$R$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />. The number of such (different) rectangles is:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/5/f657510cbc4375e2c750db19302c54aa298d0d3e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 1\\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 2 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 4 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ \\infty$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"357\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Using the perimeter and area formulas,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/3/f/63f988fc273c15da532158a22c23bc2ec1a34920.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[2(x+y) = \\frac{2}{3}(a+b)\\]\" width=\"155\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/5/9/2595f6f171e1d7a5b1da466fc08c0fc6cb12a4d0.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[x+y = \\frac{a+b}{3}\\]\" width=\"108\" height=\"37\" />\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/0/1/40122ddf962b6b3dedbb274aceb83839c1c5223c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[xy = \\frac{ab}{3}\\]\" width=\"63\" height=\"37\" />\nDividing the second equation by the last equation results in\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/3/0/830d7192c76533da945e3e9b3e76084cd505611c.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\frac1y + \\frac1x = \\frac1b + \\frac1a\\]\" width=\"119\" height=\"40\" />\nSince <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/a/e7a1884a855113f5b1058facb9b0891329d89aff.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x,y &lt; a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"62\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/c/96c260b440fe6f03010da30bc1842350ac48a352.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac1a &lt; \\tfrac1x, \\tfrac1y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -8px\" width=\"64\" height=\"23\" />.  Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/f/55f8abc0d69ac6ab491f6125f9550af6b25e22fb.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a &lt; b$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/d/8/cd8856f40c6677fc0cfc8589d55e16eb80846e30.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\tfrac1b &lt; \\tfrac1a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"44\" height=\"21\" />.  That means\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/e/2/1e2e842d0e90932409d72b552a04735cf68982c4.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\tfrac1x + \\tfrac1y &gt; \\tfrac1a + \\tfrac1a &gt; \\tfrac1a + \\tfrac1b\\]\" width=\"178\" height=\"24\" />\nThis is a contradiction, so there are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/3/5d3da52b01338a780e88792a26c3f95dc74f44f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(A)}\\ 0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"55\" height=\"28\" /> rectangles that satisfy the conditions.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME\" title=\"1963 AHSME\">1963 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1963 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1963\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 31\">Problem 31</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_33\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 33\">Problem 33</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1963 AHSME Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1963_AHSME_Problem